IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 357 (names of companies to be registered under this Part) and s 358 (application for registration),
-- lines 23188 to 23244 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- What the text hands elsewhere is an input named for the fact: section 27 (the reservation of a name, later wave), the prescribed form,
-- manner, particulars, documents and fee (regulations), and "certified" (the keel's s 4(1) "certified").

§ `The party of the rules before registration`

-- Before registration the body is a foreign corporate entity, not yet a company, so the core's `Company` does not fit it
-- (NEEDS-CORE.md: a Party constructor for a body corporate incorporated outside Singapore that intends to be registered).
DECLARE `s 357 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` HAS `the name of the foreign corporate entity` IS A STRING

DECLARE `s 357 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 357(1) apply to reserve the name of the intended company`
    `s 358(1) apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares`

§ `Section 357(1): the duty to apply to reserve the name`

-- "A foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act must apply to reserve the name
-- of the intended company." The relative clause names the class that is bound; outside it the text says nothing.
-- src:23190 | 357.—(1) A foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered
-- src:23191 | as a company limited by shares under this Act must apply to reserve
-- src:23192 | the name of the intended company.
@ref s 357(1) (src:23190-23192)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporate entity intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign corporate entity` AND `the foreign corporate entity intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act must apply": the duty is addressed to the class the relative clause names (a scope limit with no "only", the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); fork line F-357-1 in NOTES.md)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text states no time limit and no consequence, so no trace can show it breached
-- (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sge)").
@ref s 357(1) (src:23190-23192)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign corporate entity` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 357 party` `s 357 act`
`s 357(1) a foreign corporate entity that intends to be registered must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` MEANS
    PARTY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` `the name of the foreign corporate entity`
    MUST `s 357(1) apply to reserve the name of the intended company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 357(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` `the name of the foreign corporate entity` BECAUSE "the foreign corporate entity did not apply to reserve the name of the intended company" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Section 357(2): section 27 applies to the application`

-- Section 27 (the reservation of a name) is a later-wave provision and is not encoded here: this function says only that it applies.
-- src:23199 | (2) Section 27 applies to and in respect of an application under
-- src:23200 | subsection (1) as if it were an application to reserve the name of an
-- src:23201 | intended company under that section.
@ref s 357(2) (src:23199-23201)
GIVEN `the application is an application under section 357(1) to reserve the name of an intended company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(2) section 27 applies to and in respect of the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application under section 357(1) to reserve the name of an intended company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Section 27 applies to and in respect of an application under subsection (1) as if it were an application to reserve the name of an intended company under that section" speaks only of an application under subsection (1)

§ `Section 357(3): no registration without a reserved name`

-- "A foreign corporate entity must not be registered under section 359(1) unless the name which it is proposed to be registered has been
-- reserved under section 27, as applied by subsection (2)." A bar: JUST TRUE is "the subsection bars the registration".
-- When the name has been reserved the "unless" is met and the subsection does not bar (JUST FALSE); that does not say the entity may be
-- registered, which section 359(1) and section 360 decide (fork line F-357-3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:23205 | (3) A foreign corporate entity must not be registered under
-- src:23206 | section 359(1) unless the name which it is proposed to be
-- src:23207 | registered has been reserved under section 27, as applied by
-- src:23208 | subsection (2).
@ref s 357(3) (src:23205-23208)
GIVEN `the name that the foreign corporate entity is proposed to be registered under has been reserved under section 27, as applied by section 357(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357(3) the subsection bars the registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` MEANS
    IF `the name that the foreign corporate entity is proposed to be registered under has been reserved under section 27, as applied by section 357(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be registered under section 359(1) unless the name ... has been reserved": once the "unless" is met the bar does not apply
    ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the flat negative itself: "A foreign corporate entity must not be registered under section 359(1) unless ..."

§ `Section 358(1): the entity may apply to the Registrar`

-- "A foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act." A grant.
-- src:23214 | 358.—(1) A foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to
-- src:23215 | be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act.
@ref s 358(1) (src:23214-23215)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(1) the foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign corporate entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("A foreign corporate entity may apply") to the class it names; for any other body it grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-358-1 in NOTES.md)

@ref s 358(1) (src:23214-23215)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign corporate entity` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 357 party` `s 357 act`
`s 358(1) a foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered` MEANS
    PARTY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` `the name of the foreign corporate entity`
    MAY `s 358(1) apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 358(2): what the application must contain and be accompanied by`

-- The facts about one application. A record, so that the paragraphs below each read the facts they need and a seat builds it from plain answers.
-- The form, manner, particulars, other documents and fee are "as may be prescribed": the person says whether they are, never what they are.
DECLARE `s 358(2) application` HAS
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a) "must be made in such form and manner, and contain such particulars, as may be prescribed". A "must" requirement: the provision's own question.
-- src:23219 | (2) An application under subsection (1) —
-- src:23221 | (a) must be made in such form and manner, and contain such
-- src:23222 | particulars, as may be prescribed; and
@ref s 358(2)(a) (src:23219-23222)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` MEANS
    IF    application's `the application is made in the form that is prescribed`
      AND application's `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed`
      AND application's `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1) — (a) must be made in such form and manner, and contain such particulars, as may be prescribed" (a "must" requirement the application does not meet)

-- (b)(i) "a certified copy of the charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument constituting or defining its
-- constitution (if any), in its place of incorporation". "(if any)": where the entity has no such instrument there is nothing to copy.
-- src:23224 | (b) must be accompanied by —
-- src:23226 | (i) a certified copy of the charter, statute, constitution or
-- src:23227 | memorandum or articles or other instrument
-- src:23228 | constituting or defining its constitution (if any), in
-- src:23229 | its place of incorporation;
@ref s 358(2)(b)(i) (src:23224-23229)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` MEANS
    IF (NOT application's `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph asks for a copy of the instrument "(if any)": with none, nothing is owed (fork line F-358-2 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF    application's `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application`
             AND `s 4(1) "certified" the copy or translation is certified` (application's `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by — (i) a certified copy of the charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument ... (if any)" ("certified" is s 4(1)'s: certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy)

-- (b)(ii) "the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered".
-- src:23231 | (ii) the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity
-- src:23232 | proposes to be registered;
@ref s 358(2)(b)(ii) (src:23231-23232)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(b)(ii) the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` MEANS
    IF application's `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by — (ii) the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered"

-- (b)(iii) "such other documents as may be prescribed". The regulations are not a source; the person says whether every document prescribed is there.
-- src:23234 | (iii) such other documents as may be prescribed; and
@ref s 358(2)(b)(iii) (src:23234-23234)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(b)(iii) such other documents as may be prescribed accompany the application` MEANS
    IF application's `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by — (iii) such other documents as may be prescribed"

-- (b)(iv) "the prescribed fee". The Act leaves the amount to regulations and nothing here computes with it, so the fact is whether it accompanies.
-- src:23236 | (iv) the prescribed fee.
@ref s 358(2)(b)(iv) (src:23236-23236)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(b)(iv) the prescribed fee accompanies the application` MEANS
    IF application's `the prescribed fee accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by — (iv) the prescribed fee"

-- (b) all four together; (2) both paragraphs together.
-- src:23224 | (b) must be accompanied by —
@ref s 358(2)(b) (src:23224-23224)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 358(2)(b)(ii) the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 358(2)(b)(iii) such other documents as may be prescribed accompany the application` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 358(2)(b)(iv) the prescribed fee accompanies the application` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1) — ... (b) must be accompanied by — (i) ...; (ii) ...; (iii) ...; and (iv) ..."

-- src:23219 | (2) An application under subsection (1) —
-- src:23224 | (b) must be accompanied by —
@ref s 358(2) (src:23219-23224)
GIVEN application IS A `s 358(2) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF    `s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` application EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1) — (a) must be made ...; and (b) must be accompanied by ..."

§ `Section 358(3): further information or documents`

-- "The Registrar may require an applicant to furnish to the Registrar such further information or documents as the Registrar may require."
-- What it means to the applicant: it can be required to furnish more. The extent is the Registrar's judgment and is not asked here.
-- src:23240 | (3) The Registrar may require an applicant to furnish to the
-- src:23241 | Registrar such further information or documents as the Registrar may
-- src:23242 | require.
@ref s 358(3) (src:23240-23242)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant for registration under section 358(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358(3) the Registrar may require the applicant to furnish further information or documents` MEANS
    IF `the person is an applicant for registration under section 358(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power over "an applicant" ("The Registrar may require an applicant to furnish"); for anyone else it grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-358-3 in NOTES.md)
